# Chakra v2 theme

- Chakra UI v2 only (`extendTheme`, `ComponentStyleConfig`, `createMultiStyleConfigHelpers`). Never use v3 APIs (`createSystem`, `defineRecipe`, `Dialog`, `Field`) or Tailwind.
- Theme lives in `src/theme/` following Chakra's recommended structure: `index.ts`, `styles.ts`, `foundations/`, `components/` (one file per component).
- Visual reference is Midday: `reference/midday/packages/ui`. Read `src/globals.css`, `tailwind.config.ts` and the matching component file before styling a Chakra component.
- Colors go in `semanticTokens` with light and `_dark` values. No hardcoded hex values or Chakra palette colors (`gray.800` etc.) in component files.
- Midday style: monochrome, square-cornered buttons (radius 0), pills only for badges, tags and avatars, Hedvig Letters Sans/Serif, subtle focus ring, red only for destructive.
- Max font weight is 400 (Hedvig has a single weight). Use size and color for hierarchy, never bold.
- Headings use Hedvig Letters Serif. Body, UI, and mono stay Hedvig Letters Sans.
- Radii scale is all zero; use full only for avatar/switch/radio/slider thumb/pills and subtle only for modal/drawer.
- Interaction states: hover = 90% bg via color-mix, active = 80%, disabled = opacity 0.5 with no hover/active. Ghost/outline hover uses accent.
- Field focus (inputs, selects, textareas, and future form controls): border color changes to focus-border, no box shadow, no layout shift. Buttons keep the offset ring.
- Ignore colorScheme in component styles; color comes from variants and semantic tokens only.
- Keep Chakra's variant names; add new variants rather than renaming.
- Check whether a component is multipart before overriding it. If it is, use `createMultiStyleConfigHelpers` with its parts.
- Stories live in `src/stories/chakra`, use the title prefix `Chakra v2/`, and show all variants, sizes and states in light and dark mode.
